            <div xml:id="d878">

                <pb facs="0704" n="588" xml:id="pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12907.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister to
                        Mexico to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 17, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>130. Your 206. I have received the following from Mr. Fabela, Acting Secretary
                    for Foreign Affairs of General Carranza: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Duly instructed by the First Constitutionalist Chief, Senor Venustiano
                            Carranza, I beg you to convey to the Honorable W. J. Bryan, Secretary of
                            State of the United States, the sincere appreciation of Senor Carranza
                            for his congratulations sent to him through your worthy channel on
                            account of the end of our struggle and peaceful occupation of the City
                            of Mexico, and also for the desire expressed by his excellency Mr. Bryan
                            in his message to you of the 13th instant for the entering of Mexico
                            into a new era of peace, prosperity, and progress. Senor Carranza
                            sincerely esteems the desire of the Secretary of State and trusts that
                            the Mexican people, who have patriotically won their rights, will be
                            able to preserve peace in the Republic and finally enter into an era of
                            freedom and progress.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
